    Border fills row 0, row 6, and every 6th column (cols 0,6,12,18,24).
  colors:
    border: any color, must differ from tile_bg
    tile_bg: any color; shared by all 4 tiles as majority color
    cue_color, t1_color, t2_color: each a single distinct non-bg color; all 3 mutually distinct and distinct from tile_bg
  tile0_cue:
    total_pixels: 6 (single cue_color) [observed]
    wall: 5 cue pixels forming an 8-connected path through center (2,2), touching >=2 sides of the 5x5 grid
    indicator: 1 cue pixel, 8-isolated (no 8-neighbor is also cue), marks the "inside" region for tile1
    indicator_position: must be at a tile corner {(0,0),(0,4),(4,0),(4,4)} or edge midpoint {(0,2),(2,0),(2,4),(4,2)}
    wall_shapes: row, col, diag, anti-diag, or L-shape bends — must be symmetric about the line from indicator to tile center (2,2)
  tile1_pattern: 5x5 single-color pattern, 8-12 non-bg pixels, symmetric (D1+D2 or higher) [observed]
  tile2_pattern: 5x5 single-color pattern, 9-12 non-bg pixels, symmetric (D1+D2 or higher) [observed]
  tile3_input: all tile_bg (blank)
  tile3_output:
    flood-fill (4-conn) from indicator, blocked by wall → inside region
    inside pixels → tile1 non-bg; outside pixels → tile2 non-bg
    wall pixels → tile1 non-bg if present; tile2 fallback only when wall is 4-connected (axis-aligned)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 4-5 distinct colors for border, tile_bg, cue_color, t1_color, t2_color. border must differ from tile_bg.
    2. Generate tile1 and tile2 as 5x5 patterns each with a single non-bg color and some symmetry. Ensure 6-12 non-bg pixels each.
    3. Pick indicator at a tile corner or edge midpoint.
    4. Build the wall as an 8-connected path of 5 cue pixels through (2,2), symmetric about the line from indicator to (2,2).
       Options: straight line (row/col/diag/anti), or L-shape bend at (2,2).
    5. Verify: indicator is 8-isolated from wall; flood-fill (4-conn) from indicator blocked by wall produces non-empty inside AND outside.
    5. Composite tile3_output: inside → tile1 non-bg; outside → tile2 non-bg;
       wall → tile1 if non-bg, else tile2 if wall is 4-connected.
    6. Set tile3_input to all tile_bg.
    7. Assemble the 7x25 grid with border separators and tiles 0-3.
```
